{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-clax-run-site-origins-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:16:11.821217Z","id":"e94a85bd760448cfe78f1b191b2c9b88d57e3650b72908e016ef3fb349b1c086","body":{"detail":"Every artifact on one origin shares cookies, storage, service workers and CORS identity; the sandbox's opaque origin gives a site no storage at all. Neither lets artifacts be whole sites without one reaching another. A host per artifact is the browser's own isolation unit.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":88},"end":{"line":108},"content_hash":"87f0962eb4a2a6cb76e67ba4845ca0ade9c4644b6aaa784b51b44e3fd47535f5"},"summary":"Keep one shared content origin and isolate artifacts by path or by the sandboxed opaque origin","tags":["revisit:browsers gain a per-path or per-frame isolation primitive with its own storage","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-clax-run-site-origins-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:16:11.821275Z","id":"77e156cc37f42481ca98b7304962d75d82d2f8d1d057d7ccd87a2cda645c3489","body":{"detail":"A site served at its host's root cannot carry a key in every root-relative URL, and any URL credential leaks through copies, history and logs and outlives a revoked right until it expires. A server-side site session checked on every request ends with the right.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":149},"end":{"line":197},"content_hash":"3121d36a5bb84e2a883c48cd6c2c5384298ec76a54c589e087d79ba4f2b6a20c"},"summary":"Expiring signed URLs (a short-lived key in the path or query) as the credential for private content","tags":["revisit:a site needs to be embedded where no cookie can be set or sent","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-clax-run-site-origins-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:16:11.821305Z","id":"11d5e1a2b52fb030867caf9a6401187348ac8e699d7b12127038972e12fbbb32","body":{"detail":"Each version would be its own origin with its own storage, so a reviewer of an older version sees none of the app's data, and the PSL entry, certificate and handshake multiply per version. Versions under /_clax/v/<n>/ on the one origin keep one storage per artifact.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":109},"end":{"line":148},"content_hash":"62ace5ca37c787b9887f9f49cc458cb04ed206962bcb927d68af4d2744264e95"},"summary":"A host per version (v<n>--<id>.clax.run) so older versions and drafts load from their host's root","tags":["revisit:reviewers need older versions isolated from the live site's data","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-clax-run-site-origins-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:16:11.821329Z","id":"8fcbc3a19ccfb7ad79a59540e83d1fc54f183146521f57e9326078b6318454d3","body":{"detail":"The isolation would rest on every query and check being right, next to people, sessions and rights; one app's load and size would fall on the instance everyone shares. A store per artifact makes the boundary structural.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":248},"end":{"line":270},"content_hash":"0779843f0a0e5487ef899f5c000fe650f64b922f1c5c23582b9919d1fa97cc77"},"summary":"Keep app documents in the instance database behind stricter rights checks","tags":["revisit:per-artifact Durable Objects cost more than the instance can absorb at the artifact counts reached","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-clax-run-site-origins-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:16:11.821356Z","id":"acfbdeeca2690e2db3065621f6182e2c6c3bb1ad53d0e7537adf72ec6da1cf64","body":{"detail":"A top-level site has no shell to ask, and the shell would act with the viewer's clax.dev authority on an untrusted page's behalf. The runtime on the artifact's own host is scoped by that host to one artifact.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":212},"end":{"line":247},"content_hash":"c24bb4e91fbf6513374019967ebb3f057427a50bfbe8ad31ac698c788b6a73c0"},"summary":"Keep the page runtime in the clax.dev shell and reach it through postMessage from the framed site","tags":["revisit:top-level sites are dropped as a goal","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-clax-run-site-origins-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:16:11.821381Z","id":"b596c329b6eb99f3d0cfbdff72a1ab3d9a1e16501fd2c58a366cdcd0a895f52c","body":{"detail":"Before the PSL entry ships in browsers, one <id>.clax.run can set Domain=clax.run cookies its siblings receive, and SameSite does not separate them. The platform's own cookies are host-only __Host- names, so this exposes artifacts' own cookies to cookie tossing from a hostile sibling, not clax.dev's session or the site sessions. Accepted because the PSL entry is external and slow and the exposure is bounded to cookies an app sets itself.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":328},"end":{"line":334},"content_hash":"8b91b8b16c6186fd643af9b25e69ad67181009f18d016a7749a0112d9a23503a"},"summary":"Until clax.run is on the Public Suffix List, sibling artifacts are same-site to the browser","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-clax-run-site-origins-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T16:04:20.361176Z","id":"dc6c2e5a9c2226279e20b931ddf260ad6c1376f70f30d1b600271b48fbb28a41","body":{"detail":"Each version would be its own origin with its own storage, so a reviewer of an older version sees none of the app's data, and the PSL entry, certificate and handshake multiply per version. Versions under /_clax/v/<n>/ on the one origin keep one storage per artifact.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":109},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"4699a176835f0d5b7b12e7e2bf30b29737832138739508267a4b8bff46cc0b82"},"summary":"A host per version (v<n>--<id>.clax.run) so older versions and drafts load from their host's root","supersedes":"11d5e1a2b52fb030867caf9a6401187348ac8e699d7b12127038972e12fbbb32","tags":["revisit:reviewers need older versions isolated from the live site's data","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:13:00.458484Z","id":"7ce28cf1bf1e4f83e1149d43dc74bd77216cf2c05bd0ffd16e814ad3d3a4c5d3","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the owner decided the hosted account is authoritative for publication (row D2). Key linking would keep trust in the bundle (any linked key may update) and let the remote revoke a lost device's key, but it adds a key registry and verified-key UI on the remote, and editors (D7) would need their keys linked too. A third option, syncing one key through iCloud Keychain / Google Password Manager, spans Apple and Android poorly. Leaving each device a separate author makes a second device fork-only.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":83},"end":{"line":83},"content_hash":"5535ade66a143ebb4a9ae98d5ea2a2c76454241e5ef9d3c1ed41433743f137bf"},"summary":"Link each install's Ed25519 sharing key to the clax.dev account instead of making the account authoritative","tags":["revisit:bundles must be trusted without the hosted Clax, e.g. offline update between devices","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:13:00.458563Z","id":"990dd9d6a54758d4c08e2bbade54ab98b037bb8d6c4456d07810a19f8829fef5","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the owner chose Restricted on first publish, with sharing through the hosted Clax's existing roles and general access (row D4), so the app and the web share one setting. A link-by-default publish is faster to share but makes every publish public to whoever gets the address.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":85},"end":{"line":85},"content_hash":"b7efa4af3b0f088bfa1e8b9fe42cc26759977441016f427b31d92c5ffc61776c"},"summary":"Publish as Anyone with the link by default, or give the app its own visibility setting","tags":["revisit:people routinely share right after publishing and the extra Share step shows up as drop-off","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:13:00.458601Z","id":"abe07298394e477b7696a24ec0c349f509d5c61e0b51afa729177208303f7801","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the owner chose comments off by default (row D4a). The per-app Comments switch is layered on top of the roles, so Can comment acts as Can view until it is on; the alternative reading, defaulting every role and link to Can view with no switch, would need no new remote flag but loses the one-tap off for an app already shared.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":86},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"45543e0e3522ae3f38471261fceb4074c34fd5ccbed816802e845824edd74a48"},"summary":"Comments on by default, following the sharing roles alone","tags":["revisit:the per-artifact comments flag proves confusing beside the Can comment role","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:13:00.458634Z","id":"2c71a2f17fcaf69d6bf5db9bb75ec1cbd0b97df5c31b0031526a38f8f6b3819d","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the owner chose that web edits diverge (row D8), keeping public::push's moved refusal unchanged. Pulling web versions as updates would avoid Diverged after every web edit but needs a bundle-less update path; remote-built bundles would add bundle building on the Worker and drop device signatures; forbidding web edits would contradict Can edit (D7).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":90},"end":{"line":90},"content_hash":"301df963c7f1adfc509beed909c082a2988b6e5e143857348e6442f8b3556948"},"summary":"Let author devices pull web-made versions as updates, or have the remote build bundles, or forbid web edits of apps","tags":["revisit:editors publish from the web often enough that Diverged becomes the common case","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:13:00.458671Z","id":"f12f25e988bda25f904beb42ff774d79a0e5e944c1834d4f887d6208ab490532","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the remote stores bundles unread (size cap only) and every recipient runs the existing Dart read checks plus a content-hash match against the public version. A Rust reader (strict zip, manifest rules, strict Ed25519, running on wasm32 in crates/clax-worker) would duplicate apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/ and add no safety recipients do not already enforce; it would let the remote refuse a bad bundle at push time rather than at each install.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":200},"end":{"line":207},"content_hash":"9f8e7e404bae8a68fd65a589fadc7f235339627547ead734775000886fe5f6b6"},"summary":"Verify bundles on the remote with a Rust bundle reader","tags":["revisit:a non-app client (web install, CLI) downloads bundles without running the Dart reader","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:13:00.458707Z","id":"4b0256f3456b3b2b020656d0538e969ae5f95fb5d2a2113568663cbef50829cc","body":{"detail":"Not taken: push and thread sync in crates/clax-server/src/public.rs and linked.rs read the token from clax_store::remotes (remote_token); moving it to Keychain/Keystore would mean passing it into the core on each call and changing remotes.rs for the app alone. The app's embedded home is in its private support directory.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":151},"end":{"line":156},"content_hash":"295af84c525110cc8ff201a42c6c0d550acb5d2a75d8e950e2b16a79c7672b26"},"summary":"Keep the remote token in platform secure storage instead of the embedded core's store","tags":["revisit:the platform's threat model requires credentials outside app-private files (e.g. device backups include the support directory)","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-26-quickstart-onboarding-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-26T18:53:23.637867Z","id":"6570249723bdcc404ad1e29204ca3a72b6d1fb30f507a31bb83cb5b28eeb80e4","body":{"detail":"Section 5.4 sends the top window to /auth/github?next=<artifact path>. A world visitor's page runs on the site domain (site_access, crates/clax-worker), not the public origin, so the session cookie the sign-in sets may not reach the site. Decide whether 5.4 needs a site hand-off (as /_clax/session?code=&next= does in crates/clax-server/src/routes/site.rs:114) before building it.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":276},"end":{"line":279},"content_hash":"ab94da118f6625a5fb156ae214deb696917dd4f5cabaab580d93fd904ef24b77"},"summary":"Hosted account.signIn: does a world visitor's site see the new session after /auth/github, or does it need its own hand-off?","tags":["status:needs-decision","quickstart","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-26-quickstart-onboarding-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-26T18:53:23.637921Z","id":"9dc784717c2bf6d6e4b7f283d893654dafede15f66f5ebded8099ce2ceb709fd","body":{"detail":"Options: (a) clax.dev is the only default and other origins need {\"account\": {\"origins\": [...]}} in clax.json; (b) any origin, with the shell's consent naming it. (a) keeps a page from steering the owner to an unknown public Clax.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":280},"end":{"line":281},"content_hash":"cff9aee04b7588c837876bc8008a35fd224b78e62b2b6b360decc838fc471697"},"summary":"Local account.signIn: may a page sign in to an origin other than clax.dev when it declares no origins?","tags":["status:needs-decision","quickstart","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-26-quickstart-onboarding-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-26T18:53:23.637946Z","id":"5258a719fba506da4a479aefda3ce5d368211e19702615d9652093652d139606","body":{"detail":"Without it, a page that only shows \"signed in\" must declare account and so ask for the sign-in permission it never uses.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":282},"end":{"line":282},"content_hash":"38d672f8cda001240d22f9373de6f603c57beffd900f2cd53541967855d7ccaf"},"summary":"Should account.status() work without declaring account, like user.isOwner()?","tags":["status:needs-decision","quickstart","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-26-quickstart-onboarding-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-26T18:53:23.637967Z","id":"aafa9274d005fc0f50a3a4a5e37abb67e3b6d24f8f7cb72b031a7b4c23cd4906","body":{"detail":"Section 7 skips approval of a first version published by the owner or the owner's agents, since they chose the declaration. Asking once for every artifact matches iOS and Android more closely, at the cost of a prompt on every page an agent makes.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":283},"end":{"line":284},"content_hash":"ea4c556c607655834b18ab17bdebcaed374df2d5c8fada0a3ab9af817774e119"},"summary":"Permissions: should the owner's and their agents' first versions skip approval, or should every artifact ask once?","tags":["status:needs-decision","quickstart","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-26-quickstart-onboarding-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-26T18:53:23.637988Z","id":"f53d89149e185e2faaa06768b621d9832e3e9dcff692dac93278487390ffdf0b","body":{"detail":"Section 9 stops updates once the person publishes or forks a change. Comments are not changes, but a release may move or drop the elements comments are anchored to.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":285},"end":{"line":287},"content_hash":"f6644a61a1b864116bc8fd99f30d1d08d5e658734a52b7e01b9c3a6275724407"},"summary":"Seeded quickstart: keep following releases after the person comments on it, and stop only on a new version they or their agent publish?","tags":["status:needs-decision","quickstart","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-26-quickstart-onboarding-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-26T18:53:23.638007Z","id":"2e78e26f82d5dd4d76b0efe98b924b89201fa2a8ef4832fae3aacb70238fb1b3","body":{"detail":"Section 10 pushes new artifacts only (drafts excluded). The idea always-publish is still proposed; this only matters if it is accepted.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":288},"end":{"line":289},"content_hash":"c15948a6dfc1253a0ea3c8abed9d9004b621024bd58fc3221eb3a01951147a6a"},"summary":"Always publish: should turning it on also push existing artifacts?","tags":["status:needs-decision","quickstart","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-26-quickstart-onboarding-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-26T19:00:01.277328Z","id":"f6252ef5e0b1dc01730fc0a149997414103aa7964a2f1aa10996ab0b996d69c4","body":{"detail":"Chosen by the owner, 2026-10-26, over skipping approval of their own first versions. Spec section 7 now says a first version's declaration always needs approval.","kind":"comment","references":"aafa9274d005fc0f50a3a4a5e37abb67e3b6d24f8f7cb72b031a7b4c23cd4906","span":{"start":{"line":283},"end":{"line":284},"content_hash":"77a20b83ad5aeae68e18048480e891f3926f21157ba7e7da630630feca8e3091"},"summary":"Decided: every artifact asks once, the owner's and their agents' included.","tags":["status:decided","quickstart","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-26-quickstart-onboarding-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-26T19:00:01.277665Z","id":"efe20b4db9141b3d32debbe01e3295a479e662d3d38d717ef1d5504b5d9356d7","body":{"detail":"Chosen by the owner, 2026-10-26, so comments never point at elements a release moved. Spec section 9 updated.","kind":"comment","references":"f53d89149e185e2faaa06768b621d9832e3e9dcff692dac93278487390ffdf0b","span":{"start":{"line":285},"end":{"line":287},"content_hash":"0ededdb1bb4f7a187b554d384c9efc4c3951e96ad47209d4796296cf45b5be0a"},"summary":"Decided: the seeded quickstart stops following releases at the person's first activity on it, a comment or a change.","tags":["status:decided","quickstart","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.147986Z","id":"3e380119df91f2984f5bd7241c1187ee4732aa8f9aa25102a854eaa9b813e4a7","body":{"detail":"fframes 1.3.0 composites video frames itself (Frame::get_synced_video_frame with DynamicMediaProvider::with_video, https://docs.rs/fframes/1.3.0/fframes/), so one fframes Video renders cards, transitions and clips in one encode. A separate ffmpeg binary would be a second unpinned tool on macOS arm64, where no checksummed static build is published.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":343},"end":{"line":363},"content_hash":"333077edbcf878b0df5209a2d16c207faa0db870751728bd4bc4f326d054d4d5"},"summary":"An ffmpeg command line (pinned binary) to join clips, with fframes only for cards","tags":["revisit:fframes cannot decode a vignette clip's frames in sync, or its memory for one composition exceeds 8 GB","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.148054Z","id":"cfcb1b4921442baf64fdc141009c66c76d5da71b8374495b680e6d341e6620c4","body":{"detail":"A cargo genrule is simpler and avoids crate_universe annotations for ffmpeg-sys-fframes' build script, but it bypasses Bazel's cache keys for the crate graph, writes a cargo target directory of gigabytes outside Bazel's bounds (docs/bazel.md 'Disk'), and is the cargo build in a worktree AGENTS.md avoids.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":330},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"5a7a1c40543bf5da0904735031d1dc7af28c2f7581b70fc3a3ce0152b90a888f"},"summary":"Building the composer with cargo in a genrule (shared CARGO_TARGET_DIR outside the worktree) instead of a second crate_universe hub","tags":["revisit:@reel_crates makes bazel query //... fetch fframes' sources, or ffmpeg-sys-fframes' build script cannot run under rules_rust's cargo_build_script","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.148089Z","id":"6289762af378efa0005c5f1ff37e735c7e5c03ef14a1d727b0c1e71754cd982b","body":{"detail":"ffmpeg-sys-fframes 9.0.0 reads FFMPEG_BINARIES_URL (file:// accepted), so Bazel could fetch a pinned archive by sha256 and point the build script at it. Not now: the archives are keyed by target and codec features, x264 still links from the system, and the composer is a manual, never-shipped tool.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":330},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"5a7a1c40543bf5da0904735031d1dc7af28c2f7581b70fc3a3ce0152b90a888f"},"summary":"A hermetic FFmpeg for the composer (FFMPEG_BINARIES_URL at a checksummed archive Bazel fetches)","tags":["revisit:a reel render in CI fails or differs because of the downloaded FFmpeg, or the composer moves into a gating target","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.148118Z","id":"e57559e22a8f308bf85b5df132bb3d0b23cea8fded1937cd0507e44ba4b9f613","body":{"detail":"page.clock fakes Date, timers and requestAnimationFrame but not CSS animations and transitions, which would need pausing and seeking per frame through the Animation domain. Virtual time (Emulation.setVirtualTimePolicy) drives all of them at once. Kept as the fallback in plan Task 2 Step 5.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":283},"end":{"line":302},"content_hash":"898f8f2d72ecd64a3ee6549e12a0ed13377014506f0decf13913eebc4365924f"},"summary":"Playwright page.clock plus the CDP Animation domain as the deterministic clock, instead of Chromium virtual time","tags":["revisit:the shell does not paint stream or WebSocket events while virtual time is paused (plan Task 2 Step 4 fails)","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.148144Z","id":"5bcd7e19acbc8e79b08bc73b4572548c347549c9754c85eb7e94e8235819aad3","body":{"detail":"beginFrame gives compositor-exact frames but exists only in the old headless shell; the devserver vignette needs the extension and so new headless (channel: chromium, web/e2e/extension-fixtures.ts). One capture path for every vignette was preferred.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":283},"end":{"line":302},"content_hash":"898f8f2d72ecd64a3ee6549e12a0ed13377014506f0decf13913eebc4365924f"},"summary":"HeadlessExperimental.beginFrame (chrome-headless-shell, --enable-begin-frame-control) for frame-exact capture","tags":["revisit:virtual-time frames show tearing or half-painted states that beginFrame would avoid","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.148170Z","id":"803904263fb06ed0938947abae732b78d1abb0c21e036dabcaed9b72915f80a3","body":{"detail":"Live layers between people are exercised on a hosted daemon today (web/e2e/live-layers.spec.ts, presence.spec.ts: a local daemon's browsers are all its owner). LAN people would show the local shell's chrome exactly, but no test proves live layers there.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":91},"end":{"line":100},"content_hash":"59fe8012a7c39c56ccb620f2f15f4d2732bc2d3f11359ddccc93bf181fa3891f"},"summary":"A LAN person (people-helpers connect) instead of a hosted daemon for the realtime vignette","tags":["revisit:the hosted shell's chrome reads differently from a local one in the realtime or share vignette","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.148194Z","id":"0a27ab509173c7270f02d8eb1a9823587b021e882fa4336203912d1482308eba","body":{"detail":"SF Pro matches the web UI on macOS, but Apple's licence limits it to mockups of Apple platforms' UI, and a system font is not hermetic. Inter (SIL OFL 1.1) is fetched by Bazel by checksum.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":190},"end":{"line":200},"content_hash":"ddeb9c082a66708780a7c4345c0452e88f6452e241c0cd3e7ce57a8e8094f801"},"summary":"SF Pro (macOS system font) for the cards, through fframes' load_system_fonts","tags":["revisit:the owner licenses a brand typeface for Clax","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.148222Z","id":"885960f593b718a857548ab6acadf490e3d1c53450e321c4cb4178611126aec5","body":{"detail":"A published file is capped at 16 MiB (file_too_large) and is kept again in every version's content; an asset (20 MiB cap) lives outside versions and the push uploads it once (docs/contract.md 'Pushing'). Only reel.json, the small pointer, and reel.gif are files.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":504},"end":{"line":538},"content_hash":"1be5e4d9e33eab7f5d54933c81f64d74ce5441dca7469e2aa0ca1223f9adda4f"},"summary":"Publishing the video as a file of each landing-page version instead of an asset","tags":["revisit:asset storage on clax.dev is limited or priced per asset","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.148247Z","id":"0cd2db1603ccc2f6475b9f5ce229e51d46a00a119c08b1d0aedfa7dd783f3c73","body":{"detail":"A poster is a build output of the reel, which is never committed, and the binary carries only web/quickstart's SHIPPED files. Seeded copies show a link card in the page's own styles instead.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":504},"end":{"line":538},"content_hash":"1be5e4d9e33eab7f5d54933c81f64d74ce5441dca7469e2aa0ca1223f9adda4f"},"summary":"Shipping a still poster image in the binary so seeded quickstarts show a frame of the reel","tags":["revisit:the owner wants seeded galleries to show a picture of the reel","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.148272Z","id":"f168c8304e7a51bb69057e90db72d3e4513667400403f0eba0a51584a47a71a7","body":{"detail":"It is uploaded only by hand in GitHub's editor (no API), and its URL changes per upload, so the README would change at every upload. The linked GIF published as reel.gif on the landing artifact keeps one URL across uploads. Open question Q5.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":539},"end":{"line":565},"content_hash":"ff56cc5a5a1086785aefda4dc234d0a58dd419e2c451a0c502479f793a7a9400"},"summary":"A GitHub user-attachment MP4 in the README, which plays inline","tags":["revisit:the owner answers Q5 for inline playback","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.148296Z","id":"3e08196a1df7ace0bb163578d28b14eecced56252bfed35341db8aa41c24dbbe","body":{"detail":"A stable URL, but it changes only at releases, 404s when a release lacks the asset, and goes through a redirect GitHub's image proxy may not follow. The landing artifact's reel.gif changes with every upload.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":539},"end":{"line":565},"content_hash":"ff56cc5a5a1086785aefda4dc234d0a58dd419e2c451a0c502479f793a7a9400"},"summary":"Hosting the README GIF as releases/latest/download/clax-reel.gif","tags":["revisit:the landing artifact's site cannot serve reel.gif to GitHub's image proxy (spec R7)","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.148320Z","id":"84bc6e7dea99e636fcd0951047bdb91bc6a4a8a1a1d36324bd3b7a5411a78fc7","body":{"detail":"The owner's installed Clax already holds the clax.dev sign-in and the link to the public copy; asset upload, publish and push through it reuse tested paths, including the asset address rewrite, and keep the public artifact's URL stable. A direct client would need its own token handling.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":472},"end":{"line":486},"content_hash":"baa7e4126c4c042d79b5a65c837634b2c6a043d5bd8fc4be8c603f04fec80d9b"},"summary":"reel-upload talking to clax.dev's API directly with a token of its own","tags":["revisit:the landing artifact is no longer published from a local artifact the owner's Clax links","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.148343Z","id":"dcfbebd5bf163bd6ad39b2b005c92a8c8eee20029e60f0914a3c5dc5a896acc3","body":{"detail":"web/reel/reel.toml [upload] landing stays empty and scripts/reel-upload.sh refuses until this is answered; the README block (spec 11.2) and REEL_PAGE in web/quickstart/index.html need the same URL.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":611},"end":{"line":614},"content_hash":"1ddcd9a92a8cec9a9181914407f75ff8e0b8ca6b3c9e113987a6cc9eb383f522"},"summary":"Q1: which clax.dev artifact is the landing page, and which local artifact of the owner's is linked to it?","tags":["status:needs-decision","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.148367Z","id":"ca1be8c0f4933347b3c5a6f03f475e78ea6d5abafe64f090d86adba1bea3d37f","body":{"detail":"tools/reel-compose links fframes with the h264 and libav-agree-gpl features (spec 8, R2). The composer is never shipped, so the GPL does not reach Clax's binaries or the video. VideoToolbox avoids the GPL but is macOS only and its output is not bit-identical across machines.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":615},"end":{"line":617},"content_hash":"63f8b5572006d3c13a4642a452174e9c3b64d4889f48cdaa4e0e5701d360cb98"},"summary":"Q2: x264 (GPL, system library) or VideoToolbox for the composer's H.264 encode?","tags":["status:needs-decision","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.148391Z","id":"62367cde6d0e04c48fa2d356462da102b251e519a44a5c1a0c618f5253eb135a","body":{"detail":"The draft is silent. fframes mixes audio (AudioMap, AudioMixOptions), but a track needs a licence that allows the landing page and the README.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":618},"end":{"line":619},"content_hash":"1b62e4b856eb82de8b7ce3bd799327c8eabfaecd1f8ad76c50edd8d1a8bcc31d"},"summary":"Q3: a silent reel, or a music bed?","tags":["status:needs-decision","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.148413Z","id":"cab4175a82eb19514ebe3845b158b9a86d9b4662ad8a6fbba13c416f371b1cd4","body":{"detail":"A dark render doubles every vignette's render time (spec R3) and needs a second asset on the landing page chosen by prefers-color-scheme.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":620},"end":{"line":620},"content_hash":"aaeaa5e6f5242d13dab642e68f5b4411916a4bba6790ca034d5bf7f2b49b637b"},"summary":"Q4: light theme only, or a dark-theme render too?","tags":["status:needs-decision","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T14:33:58.148435Z","id":"59530f0070ed20b90ed1632dad751246ea333dd07fb4835ee3cd83a49391ad22","body":{"detail":"The draft shows reel.gif published on the landing artifact, linked to the landing page (spec 11.2); a user-attachment MP4 plays inline but is uploaded by hand at each release and changes the README each time.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":621},"end":{"line":622},"content_hash":"309ead7f07472d53daa3ede73850a82ff5328e9ab3cfbdd9d3531d1a481c1414"},"summary":"Q5: README shows a linked GIF, or a GitHub user-attachment MP4?","tags":["status:needs-decision","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:32.213668Z","id":"70c8aa05b58b65b22a069651051df44acb222d6ab380c7e4481c7a2f5afad045","body":{"detail":"Recorded in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md D8 and section 14 Q1. The clax.dev artifact ID is fixed when the Quickstart is first published, then set in web/reel/reel.toml [upload] landing_artifact and landing (spec section 9.3); the per-machine local artifact stays in ~/.config/clax/reel/upload.toml (section 10). reel-upload publishes the landing artifact as web/quickstart's files plus reel.gif, so a republish never drops the GIF (R8).","kind":"comment","references":"dcfbebd5bf163bd6ad39b2b005c92a8c8eee20029e60f0914a3c5dc5a896acc3","summary":"Decided 2026-10-27: the Clax Quickstart is the landing page; web/quickstart/ is its canonical version and the clax.dev landing artifact is published from it; reel-upload attaches the reel to that artifact.","tags":["status:decided","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:32.213994Z","id":"bc2b49396b349e96d760493182082a9df492907a1c18a1cb7483c2ea18917310","body":{"detail":"Recorded in the spec's D9, R2 and section 14 Q2. x264 also keeps crf, preset and tune control and gives the same output on macOS and on the Linux CI runner; VideoToolbox is not used.","kind":"comment","references":"ca1be8c0f4933347b3c5a6f03f475e78ea6d5abafe64f090d86adba1bea3d37f","summary":"Decided 2026-10-27: x264. The GPL is acceptable because the composer is a developer tool that is never shipped.","tags":["status:decided","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:32.214264Z","id":"510413d3cd48fd059f5ed49490bc30ffccbe2f4f01824f3aa85fafcf3c600e0e","body":{"detail":"Recorded in the spec's D10 and section 14 Q3. The composer writes no audio track; a later music bed needs a licence that covers the landing page and the README.","kind":"comment","references":"62367cde6d0e04c48fa2d356462da102b251e519a44a5c1a0c618f5253eb135a","summary":"Decided 2026-10-27: silent for now; a music bed may come later.","tags":["status:decided","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:32.214515Z","id":"08b1eaee36a610fc190f0c9f27001c698f3df43f57659f37dc2e7fedeb1a562a","body":{"detail":"Recorded in the spec's D11 and section 14 Q4. A dark render stays a later addition (a second render of every vignette, and a second asset chosen by prefers-color-scheme).","kind":"comment","references":"cab4175a82eb19514ebe3845b158b9a86d9b4662ad8a6fbba13c416f371b1cd4","summary":"Decided 2026-10-27: light theme only in the first version; dark later.","tags":["status:decided","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:32.214770Z","id":"6dc6d141b4a69a366948b9a13c5d2f40039e9331d281e1a9c31d61fb76249651","body":{"detail":"Recorded in the spec's D12, D13, section 9.4, section 11.2 and section 14 Q5. The full video stays a build output (target/reel/); uploading reel.mp4 (landing-page player and release asset) is a later phase, after the GIF and the README (plan phase 3, Tasks 15 to 18).","kind":"comment","references":"59530f0070ed20b90ed1632dad751246ea333dd07fb4835ee3cd83a49391ad22","summary":"Decided 2026-10-27: the README shows a linked animated GIF, rendered independently of the video (its own 6 to 10 second loop of the strongest beats, with its own size, frame rate and palette budget), not transcoded from reel.mp4.","tags":["status:decided","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:32.215021Z","id":"cac0d0ec58c2329c495fffa504d0d894f0b5a283623ca73d11a87f8a9f52c53b","body":{"detail":"Recorded in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md D12 and section 14 Q5. The revisit condition (the owner answering Q5 for inline playback) is met with the GIF answer; the owner may close this record.","kind":"comment","references":"f168c8304e7a51bb69057e90db72d3e4513667400403f0eba0a51584a47a71a7","summary":"The owner answered Q5 on 2026-10-27: a linked animated GIF in the README; this alternative (a user-attachment MP4) was not taken.","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:32.215336Z","id":"0197dfa08a37bb5dc57b84a0f46b907776a6e69524d5e2175036181875e69046","body":{"detail":"Live layers between people are exercised on a hosted daemon today (web/e2e/live-layers.spec.ts, presence.spec.ts: a local daemon's browsers are all its owner). LAN people would show the local shell's chrome exactly, but no test proves live layers there.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":145},"content_hash":"59fe8012a7c39c56ccb620f2f15f4d2732bc2d3f11359ddccc93bf181fa3891f"},"summary":"A LAN person (people-helpers connect) instead of a hosted daemon for the realtime vignette","supersedes":"803904263fb06ed0938947abae732b78d1abb0c21e036dabcaed9b72915f80a3","tags":["revisit:the hosted shell's chrome reads differently from a local one in the realtime or share vignette","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:32.298635Z","id":"7a802873dda1afd34244af9f9cd955c3a2941ff806c797264a3871d7a401583e","body":{"detail":"SF Pro matches the web UI on macOS, but Apple's licence limits it to mockups of Apple platforms' UI, and a system font is not hermetic. Inter (SIL OFL 1.1) is fetched by Bazel by checksum.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":237},"end":{"line":247},"content_hash":"ddeb9c082a66708780a7c4345c0452e88f6452e241c0cd3e7ce57a8e8094f801"},"summary":"SF Pro (macOS system font) for the cards, through fframes' load_system_fonts","supersedes":"0a27ab509173c7270f02d8eb1a9823587b021e882fa4336203912d1482308eba","tags":["revisit:the owner licenses a brand typeface for Clax","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:32.378786Z","id":"ddaadf6229abab30c0af773b71972355362ee76b42fe744c1f12bb3de17fe42d","body":{"detail":"beginFrame gives compositor-exact frames but exists only in the old headless shell; the devserver vignette needs the extension and so new headless (channel: chromium, web/e2e/extension-fixtures.ts). One capture path for every vignette was preferred.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":330},"end":{"line":349},"content_hash":"898f8f2d72ecd64a3ee6549e12a0ed13377014506f0decf13913eebc4365924f"},"summary":"HeadlessExperimental.beginFrame (chrome-headless-shell, --enable-begin-frame-control) for frame-exact capture","supersedes":"5bcd7e19acbc8e79b08bc73b4572548c347549c9754c85eb7e94e8235819aad3","tags":["revisit:virtual-time frames show tearing or half-painted states that beginFrame would avoid","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:32.463625Z","id":"6cdafdacac739465067ff81700f540614593b58b0087c2613149f5969445f66d","body":{"detail":"page.clock fakes Date, timers and requestAnimationFrame but not CSS animations and transitions, which would need pausing and seeking per frame through the Animation domain. Virtual time (Emulation.setVirtualTimePolicy) drives all of them at once. Kept as the fallback in plan Task 2 Step 5.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":330},"end":{"line":349},"content_hash":"898f8f2d72ecd64a3ee6549e12a0ed13377014506f0decf13913eebc4365924f"},"summary":"Playwright page.clock plus the CDP Animation domain as the deterministic clock, instead of Chromium virtual time","supersedes":"e57559e22a8f308bf85b5df132bb3d0b23cea8fded1937cd0507e44ba4b9f613","tags":["revisit:the shell does not paint stream or WebSocket events while virtual time is paused (plan Task 2 Step 4 fails)","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:32.544184Z","id":"aae1bcc51151b4b3008757427f6ae6492035820ac30558d3defd983eecbb36c9","body":{"detail":"ffmpeg-sys-fframes 9.0.0 reads FFMPEG_BINARIES_URL (file:// accepted), so Bazel could fetch a pinned archive by sha256 and point the build script at it. Not now: the archives are keyed by target and codec features, x264 still links from the system, and the composer is a manual, never-shipped tool.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":378},"end":{"line":393},"content_hash":"fdf0f0e9d95ad98ba718d39e2e937f4fbc9687137642ffc165a143de2569ccf1"},"summary":"A hermetic FFmpeg for the composer (FFMPEG_BINARIES_URL at a checksummed archive Bazel fetches)","supersedes":"6289762af378efa0005c5f1ff37e735c7e5c03ef14a1d727b0c1e71754cd982b","tags":["revisit:a reel render in CI fails or differs because of the downloaded FFmpeg, or the composer moves into a gating target","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:32.624899Z","id":"8d3bfd5cd67b191fb45fb3dc74078aa6b7285494e16116b53d0305d4787e8a38","body":{"detail":"A cargo genrule is simpler and avoids crate_universe annotations for ffmpeg-sys-fframes' build script, but it bypasses Bazel's cache keys for the crate graph, writes a cargo target directory of gigabytes outside Bazel's bounds (docs/bazel.md 'Disk'), and is the cargo build in a worktree AGENTS.md avoids.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":378},"end":{"line":393},"content_hash":"fdf0f0e9d95ad98ba718d39e2e937f4fbc9687137642ffc165a143de2569ccf1"},"summary":"Building the composer with cargo in a genrule (shared CARGO_TARGET_DIR outside the worktree) instead of a second crate_universe hub","supersedes":"cfcb1b4921442baf64fdc141009c66c76d5da71b8374495b680e6d341e6620c4","tags":["revisit:@reel_crates makes bazel query //... fetch fframes' sources, or ffmpeg-sys-fframes' build script cannot run under rules_rust's cargo_build_script","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:32.705340Z","id":"22152b869de4f686eb75a2519bffdf840be9580467841a1cad6921339955a27c","body":{"detail":"fframes 1.3.0 composites video frames itself (Frame::get_synced_video_frame with DynamicMediaProvider::with_video, https://docs.rs/fframes/1.3.0/fframes/), so one fframes Video renders cards, transitions and clips in one encode. A separate ffmpeg binary would be a second unpinned tool on macOS arm64, where no checksummed static build is published.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":395},"end":{"line":416},"content_hash":"144e3c058c73dd5b4b674898b6b7fb3a9b72f05cbcb582a712aa96a15922c453"},"summary":"An ffmpeg command line (pinned binary) to join clips, with fframes only for cards","supersedes":"3e380119df91f2984f5bd7241c1187ee4732aa8f9aa25102a854eaa9b813e4a7","tags":["revisit:fframes cannot decode a vignette clip's frames in sync, or its memory for one composition exceeds 8 GB","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:32.786916Z","id":"f23a22f70a158cf4b6d4a6b8f591142cffcdce3a90c13337183e167df686077d","body":{"detail":"The owner's installed Clax already holds the clax.dev sign-in and the link to the public copy; asset upload, publish and push through it reuse tested paths, including the asset address rewrite, and keep the public artifact's URL stable. A direct client would need its own token handling.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":592},"end":{"line":611},"content_hash":"17f214ca9ce105eada46013bea07c26d3b7276c608b804e8a10b3bed2e86fefe"},"summary":"reel-upload talking to clax.dev's API directly with a token of its own","supersedes":"84bc6e7dea99e636fcd0951047bdb91bc6a4a8a1a1d36324bd3b7a5411a78fc7","tags":["revisit:the landing artifact is no longer published from a local artifact the owner's Clax links","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:32.869905Z","id":"d89cad9596a83f77a6bbe7f3b5511d3d34dc0e7e4417afb7aa2edcf60f485915","body":{"detail":"A poster is a build output of the reel, which is never committed, and the binary carries only web/quickstart's SHIPPED files. Seeded copies show a link card in the page's own styles instead.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":633},"end":{"line":673},"content_hash":"57720b87bdba4cedafb03873842b9eae5e2cd5618d42214ea6dfc6cb8558a74b"},"summary":"Shipping a still poster image in the binary so seeded quickstarts show a frame of the reel","supersedes":"0cd2db1603ccc2f6475b9f5ce229e51d46a00a119c08b1d0aedfa7dd783f3c73","tags":["revisit:the owner wants seeded galleries to show a picture of the reel","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:32.950264Z","id":"65f0a3fa136fde57366832ea363e0a5a290c36a022e7db3bac7b1f9335e44fbc","body":{"detail":"A published file is capped at 16 MiB (file_too_large) and is kept again in every version's content; an asset (20 MiB cap) lives outside versions and the push uploads it once (docs/contract.md 'Pushing'). Only reel.json, the small pointer, and reel.gif are files.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":633},"end":{"line":673},"content_hash":"57720b87bdba4cedafb03873842b9eae5e2cd5618d42214ea6dfc6cb8558a74b"},"summary":"Publishing the video as a file of each landing-page version instead of an asset","supersedes":"885960f593b718a857548ab6acadf490e3d1c53450e321c4cb4178611126aec5","tags":["revisit:asset storage on clax.dev is limited or priced per asset","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:33.030720Z","id":"53652064c92db2cf3a4a71d71a5532312c21b5ccdc2a4ec9f8817a1500530f30","body":{"detail":"A stable URL, but it changes only at releases, 404s when a release lacks the asset, and goes through a redirect GitHub's image proxy may not follow. The landing artifact's reel.gif changes with every upload.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":675},"end":{"line":697},"content_hash":"a2649a35e6acacb4356a3c04b6060aaf13d38320a18a68eff2515a758ddabad3"},"summary":"Hosting the README GIF as releases/latest/download/clax-reel.gif","supersedes":"3e08196a1df7ace0bb163578d28b14eecced56252bfed35341db8aa41c24dbbe","tags":["revisit:the landing artifact's site cannot serve reel.gif to GitHub's image proxy (spec R7)","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:33.111015Z","id":"41e51ea8b24f99a7c97679a4bd1347946be8584cde10e78fdba2ec01c8733744","body":{"detail":"It is uploaded only by hand in GitHub's editor (no API), and its URL changes per upload, so the README would change at every upload. The linked GIF published as reel.gif on the landing artifact keeps one URL across uploads. Open question Q5.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":675},"end":{"line":697},"content_hash":"a2649a35e6acacb4356a3c04b6060aaf13d38320a18a68eff2515a758ddabad3"},"summary":"A GitHub user-attachment MP4 in the README, which plays inline","supersedes":"f168c8304e7a51bb69057e90db72d3e4513667400403f0eba0a51584a47a71a7","tags":["revisit:the owner answers Q5 for inline playback","reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
